The author steps aside in their own secondary voice — notes, boxed asides, and disclosure.

<section #sh-aside | `<aside>`>

<sub-section | General Usage>

Semantic role: *aside*. Compiles to eHTML `<aside>`.

Registers:

- Canonical: `<aside>`

<code #code:sh-aside-1>
<aside | A side note about the elephant.>
</code>

<minipage #mp:sh-aside-1>
<aside | A side note about the elephant.>
</minipage>

<code #code:sh-aside-2>
<aside type=warning .important | Be careful here.>
</code>

<minipage #mp:sh-aside-2>
<aside type=warning .important | Be careful here.>
</minipage>

<code-block #code:sh-aside-3>
<aside type=callout |
This is a multi-line callout.

It can contain multiple paragraphs and other content like
<strong | emphasis> and inline references.
>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:sh-aside-3>
<aside type=callout |
This is a multi-line callout.

It can contain multiple paragraphs and other content like
<strong | emphasis> and inline references.
>
</minipage>

<sub-section | Arguments>

| attribute | kind | values / default | notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `type` | kwarg | `note` `sidebar` `callout` `warning` `tip` `info` `caution` | Optional classification of the aside's role. |
| `title` | kwarg |  | Optional title rendered at the top of the aside (the frameable title-top convention, #31). |
| `caption` | kwarg |  | Optional caption rendered at the foot of the aside (frameable caption-bottom convention, #31), with the "Box N." label folded in when numbered. |
| `+numbered` / `-numbered` | flag | default off | Whether this aside is numbered. |
| `+border` / `-border` | flag | default on | Frameable surface (#31). |

</section>

<section #sh-details | `<details>`>

<sub-section | General Usage>

Semantic role: *details*. Compiles to eHTML `<details>`.

Registers:

- Canonical: `<details>`

<code-block #code:sh-details-1>
<details>
  <summary | More background>
  Additional context for the curious reader. The summary is the
  visible heading; this body shows when the disclosure is opened.
</details>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:sh-details-1>
<details>
  <summary | More background>
  Additional context for the curious reader. The summary is the
  visible heading; this body shows when the disclosure is opened.
</details>
</minipage>

*The canonical shape: a &lt;summary&gt; for the visible heading,
followed by the disclosure body. The body is recursively parsed
as prose / block content.*

<code-block #code:sh-details-2>
<details +open>
  <summary | Always-expanded section>
  This disclosure is expanded by default.
</details>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:sh-details-2>
<details +open>
  <summary | Always-expanded section>
  This disclosure is expanded by default.
</details>
</minipage>

*The +open boolean kwarg expands the disclosure by default.
Maps to HTML's standard open attribute.*

<sub-section | Arguments>

| attribute | kind | values / default | notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `open` | kwarg | `true` `false` | HTML's open attribute on &lt;details&gt;. |

</section>

<section #sh-endnotes | `<endnotes>`>

<sub-section | General Usage>

Semantic role: *endnotes*. Compiles to eHTML `<endnotes>`.

Registers:

- Canonical: `<endnotes>`

</section>

<section #sh-note | `<note>`>

<sub-section | General Usage>

Semantic role: *note*. Compiles to eHTML `<note>`.

Registers:

- Canonical: `<note>`

<code #code:sh-note-1>
Some text<note | A substantive note about the text.>.
</code>

<minipage #mp:sh-note-1>
Some text<note | A substantive note about the text.>.
</minipage>

<code #code:sh-note-2>
A claim<note placement=foot | A footnote.>.
</code>

<minipage #mp:sh-note-2>
A claim<note placement=foot | A footnote.>.
</minipage>

<code #code:sh-note-3>
A definition<note position=margin | A margin note.>.
</code>

<minipage #mp:sh-note-3>
A definition<note position=margin | A margin note.>.
</minipage>

<sub-section | Arguments>

| attribute | kind | values / default | notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `placement` | kwarg | `end` `foot` `margin` (default `end`) | The note's position — one note type, three positions. |
| `position` | kwarg | `end` `foot` `margin` | Alias for "placement" (same values, same data-note-placement output). |
| `type` | kwarg | `substantive` `technical` `editorial` `translator` `other` (default `substantive`) | Optional classification. |

</section>

<section #sh-note-list | `<note-list>`>

<sub-section | General Usage>

Semantic role: *note-list*. Compiles to eHTML `<note-list>`.

Registers:

- Canonical: `<note-list>`

<sub-section | Arguments>

| attribute | kind | values / default | notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `type` | kwarg | `end-notes` `chapter-notes` `footnotes-collected` `other` (default `end-notes`) |  |

</section>

<section #sh-summary | `<summary>`>

<sub-section | General Usage>

Semantic role: *summary*. Compiles to eHTML `<summary>`.

Registers:

- Canonical: `<summary>`

<code #code:sh-summary-1>
<summary | More background>
</code>

<minipage #mp:sh-summary-1>
<summary | More background>
</minipage>

*The visible heading of a &lt;details&gt; disclosure. Appears as a
child of &lt;details&gt;.*

<code #code:sh-summary-2>
<summary | Click to reveal the <em | hidden> details>
</code>

<minipage #mp:sh-summary-2>
<summary | Click to reveal the <em | hidden> details>
</minipage>

*Inline markup in a summary. The recursive-content pass parses
the pipe content normally.*

</section>
